From 6c08be339e6f5c6a01db2126a9a17388696e4434 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mahak Fahad <mahak867@github>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 21:17:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix: DB_TIMEOUT from concurrent fullCloudSync calls on
 page load
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: onAuthStateChange(INITIAL_SESSION) and getSession() both fire
within ~100ms of each other on every authenticated page load. Both triggered
fullCloudSync() simultaneously, causing two concurrent Supabase queries. The
second query starved and hit the 8s timeout, throwing DB_TIMEOUT.

Confirmed in Sentry: ID cfc13039a8ad4f66a8567adcf0eceebc, May 22 2026.

Changes:
- Add _syncInFlight boolean lock to fullCloudSync(). Second caller bails
  immediately with false — no query fired, no race condition.
- Extract _timedQuery(promise, ms) helper — DRYs the timeout pattern and
  ensures the re-fetch query (after uploading local-only items) is also
  timeout-guarded. Previously only the initial fetch was guarded.
- Rename internal logic to _doFullCloudSync() — the public export is now
  purely the lock wrapper.
---
 src/collection.js | 63 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/collection.js b/src/collection.js
index 15a6c7a..ffc5f73 100644
