From 5918e8d703da29357a8d70280919e6e5c3b9e736 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mahak Fahad <mahak867@github>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 21:23:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] security: harden to production standard across all attack
 surfaces
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CRITICAL fixes:
- config.js: remove hardcoded live Razorpay key (rzp_live_*) and DEV_EMAIL
  from source. All secrets now loaded exclusively from env vars. Added
  .env.example documenting every required variable.

- auth.js/ui.js: eliminate client-side is_pro self-grant. startPayment()
  no longer writes is_pro=true to Supabase via the anon key. Pro status
  is now poll-verified from the server profile after the Razorpay webhook
  fires. isPro() no longer trusts localStorage — server profile only.

- supabase_migration.sql: patch 6 open RLS policies:
  * scan_logs insert: was check(true) → now requires auth.uid()=user_id
  * referrals insert: was check(true) → now requires auth.uid()=referred_user_id
  * profiles SELECT: was using(true) (all user data public) → own row only
  * profiles UPDATE: add WITH CHECK blocking is_pro/is_developer mutation
    from the client. Only the webhook (service role) can set these columns.
  * listings SELECT: expose a public_listings VIEW without seller_phone.
    Full data (inc. phone) only returned to the seller themselves.
  * community_prices insert: require authenticated user (block anon spam)

HIGH fixes:
- vercel.json: add full security header suite to all routes:
  * Content-Security-Policy (script-src, connect-src, frame-src scoped)
  * Strict-Transport-Security (2yr, includeSubDomains, preload)
  * X-Frame-Options: DENY
  * X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  * Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  * Permissions-Policy: camera=(self) only, no mic/geo/USB/bluetooth
  * Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups (Razorpay)
  * Cache-Control: immutable on /assets/ (missing before)
- robots.txt: created (was missing entirely, /api/ now disallowed)

MEDIUM fixes:
- index.html: remove user-scalable=no (WCAG 1.4.4 accessibility violation)
- index.html: add missing og:locale, og:site_name, color-scheme, format-detection
- marketplace.js: public listing reads use public_listings view (no phone leakage)
- marketplace.js: add rel=noopener noreferrer to cross-origin OLX link
